    21	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
    22	| **v4 (ours)** | Q4_K_M | 1,706 | **2.96** (1.7–4.6) | 1,303 | 22 |
    23	| GUI-Owl-1.5-2B | Q4_K_M | 2,228 | 7.00 (4.6–10.4) | 2,106 | 47 |
    24	| MAI-UI-2B (run in progress: 77 of 116 episodes) | Q8_0 (Q4_K_M breaks its output: results/maiui_quant_check.md) | 1,655 | 9.00 (6.0–13.4) | 2,226 | 51 |
    25	
    26	
    27	## Real phone: Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6 (Qualcomm Device Cloud)
    28	
    29	Device: Qualcomm reference phone "Art for arm64" (SM8975, Snapdragon 8 Elite Extreme Gen 6), Android SDK 37, 11474320 kB RAM. Models run ON the phone's CPU (llama.cpp b12110 = `cd959bae9`, official Android arm64 build, 4 threads, no prompt cache); the Mac only sends the same screenshots and goals through each model's own agent code and records every response.
    30	
    31	**Headline (same phone, same clock):** v4's evaluation image budget is 1,024 tokens, so its option-2 runs are also its evaluation setting; they ran at the same sampled ~2.65 GHz as GUI-Owl's and MAI-UI's option-1 runs. As evaluated, one step takes **~39.0 s for v4** vs 1100 s for GUI-Owl and 1063 s for MAI-UI (~28× and ~27×). At the same 1,024-token image budget for all three (option 2), GUI-Owl and MAI-UI take ~5.1× and ~4.7× v4's time. Option 1's v4 row ran earlier at the full 4.03 GHz, so it is not the like-for-like number.
