   123	r1 = out["round1"]["v4"]
   124	pr = out["round1"].get("maiui_q4_fa_probe") or {}
   125	L += ["", f"Round 1 (earlier the same day, default flash-attention setting, 3 timed passes): v4 completed all {r1['calls']} timed calls, "
   126	      f"median {r1['e2e_median_s']} s end-to-end ({r1['phone_median_s']} s on the phone). GUI-Owl's and MAI-UI's first calls never "
   127	      "completed before their client gave up (MobileWorld's 120 s timeout plus re-sends), so round 2 used one long timeout without "
   128	      f"re-sends for every model. A single MAI-UI Q4_K_M probe with flash attention took {pr.get('e2e_s')} s ({pr.get('prompt_s')} s "
   129	      f"on the prompt) and ended in a {pr.get('gen_tokens')}-token degenerate output (finish reason `{pr.get('finish_reason')}`).",
   130	      "", "The phone slowed under sustained load: after about two hours the sampled fastest-core frequency had fallen from "
   131	      "4.03 GHz to about 2.65 GHz and v4's same screenshots went from ~27 s to ~38 s; that is why option 2 runs the models in "
